 "best_idea": "Store worn gear as a map from slot name to one item-instance id, make equip a toggle, and save and restore that map per deck by id, so a loadout is a few ids and not copies of items.",
 "decision": "adapt",
 "decision_why": "The slot map and by-id loadouts fit gear dressing (row 15) and the one-ledger ruling; we keep the toggle and the per-deck loadouts, but a missing id becomes a logged refusal, the displaced item's flag is cleared, and the random defeat crack is not ported as a default.",
 "decision_status": "proposed",
 "acceptance": "A player taps a worn Body item, which comes off; taps a second Body item, and the first returns to the bag; a server test asserts that after a deck switch with bound loadouts each slot holds the id saved for that deck, and a saved id that no longer exists is reported in the log, not skipped silently."
